"""MISHRI — real Bazel build entry point.

Founder real-time: "MISHRI forked from an unknown author please update it to build with bazel and
also the artifacts to include a construct file the concatination check parena editor out for an
example." Same real, pragmatic "no external bazel_dep until something real needs one" precedent
PARENA's own MODULE.bazel already established -- this repo's own real, hermetic-and-sandboxable
piece (the humanness-layer unit test, tests/humanness.test.js) needs nothing beyond plain Node.js
built-ins, so no rules_nodejs/aspect_rules_js toolchain is pulled in. The `npm install`/`npm start`
side of this project (real mineflayer network deps) is deliberately NOT wrapped as a hermetic
Bazel build/test action -- see BUILD.bazel's own doc comment on :install/:run for why, and
scripts/README-equivalent npm workflow for the real, normal way to run the bot itself.
"""

module(
    name = "mishri",
    version = "1.0.0",
)

# rules_shell -- Bazel 8+'s own real split: sh_binary/sh_test/sh_library are no longer Starlark
# globals, a real BCR dependency now (found live: `bazel build` failed with "name 'sh_test' is
# not defined" until this was added).
bazel_dep(name = "rules_shell", version = "0.6.1")
